{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question","id":455129,"title":"A Spirit Question..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-23T18:27:35-07:00","id":455129,"title":"A Spirit Question..","content":"Earlier today, I briefly forgot that Wolf Gifts are automatically unlocked, and I was wondering what kind of spirits you would need to hunt down to get Luna's Embrace (Change; Honor).<br /> <br /> Then I got to wondering... are there Spirits of gender? Like, Spirits with Influence (Man) or Influence (Woman)? Or would that be covered under the whole &quot;there are no Spirits of Humanity&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Similarly, would there be Spirits of things like Faces (which are something that's almost by definition restricted to humans) or of attributes (Strength, Beauty, Honor, etc)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T18:36:59-07:00","id":455176,"title":"","content":"I was wondering something similar. How close to humanity can you get? There are ancestral spirits, are they only a werewolf thing? Would there be a spirit of, say, Abraham Lincoln? What about the Lincoln Memorial? Spirits of brotherhood and sisterhood? A 'father' spirit? A 'mother?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-23-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:06:06-07:00","id":455225,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I would argue that ancestral spirits are a werewolf thing, unless you wanted to dive into the Underworld or get a Mage involved. Abraham Lincoln wouldn't have a spirit, but probably wouldn't have a ghost either- he'd likely have the Temenos being discussed in <b>Astral Realms </b>called a Walker; which if I'm understanding correctly is an amalgamation of hundreds of people's perception of a famous person. I think Mage even mentions some famous people being possessed by their own Walkers during their lifetime. A spirit of the Lincoln Memorial would make sense, since it's a place, not a person. I'd also suggest that spirits of relationships like brotherhood, sisterhood, fathers, and mothers exist. Those identities are not just human-specific. They have also been seen to apply to great apes, cetaceans, and elephants. And even if they didn't count enough to make the emotion, or if it was too human, werewolves feel those emotions too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:12:19-07:00","id":455231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question#post455129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier today, I briefly forgot that Wolf Gifts are automatically unlocked, and I was wondering what kind of spirits you would need to hunt down to get Luna's Embrace (Change; Honor).</div> </div> </div> </div>None, those gifts are already unlocked as you said. They are already carved in each Uratha, so you only need to pay 1 experience to unlock the facet, assuming you have at least one dot of Honor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question#post455129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I got to wondering... are there Spirits of gender? Like, Spirits with Influence (Man) or Influence (Woman)? Or would that be covered under the whole &quot;there are no Spirits of Humanity&quot; thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably have spiritual manifestations of gender roles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question#post455129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, would there be Spirits of things like Faces (which are something that's almost by definition restricted to humans) or of attributes (Strength, Beauty, Honor, etc)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Define 'Faces' here. You mean like... a person's face? If that's the case, such a face would need to be pretty iconic, think Che Guevara shirts iconic.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yes, you do have spirits of those abstract concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T19:31:25-07:00","id":455250,"title":"","content":"Uncle Sam? Ronald McDonald? Clowns? It seems like occupational spirits would exist, so you could have a mailperson spirit or a cop spirit, a soldier spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T01:30:07-07:00","id":455544,"title":"","content":"I think those are covered by spirits of delivery, laws and war, respectively. <br /> <br /> I think the question really depends on what exactly happened to our spiritual reflection. Did we just become so complex that there ceased to be an &quot;archetypal&quot; human to define? Did we sever it or merge with it in some sort of ritual for power? If it's the former then yeah, every aspect of humanity should be represented somehow, but if it's the latter then who knows how much of what defines us got removed from the Hisil ecosystem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T05:25:18-07:00","id":455704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455544#post455544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those are covered by spirits of delivery, laws and war, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems needlessly reductive. Especially since a mailperson doesn't deliver jokes, and cops are certainly more than a component of the law, and their aspect in the Hisil would show that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the question really depends on what exactly happened to our spiritual reflection. Did we just become so complex that there ceased to be an &quot;archetypal&quot; human to define? Did we sever it or merge with it in some sort of ritual for power? If it's the former then yeah, every aspect of humanity should be represented somehow, but if it's the latter then who knows how much of what defines us got removed from the Hisil ecosystem. </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably sure we'll never get an answer to that question unless there's an entirely new new World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-24-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T05:56:31-07:00","id":455740,"title":"","content":"That's true enough, but I still think it could potentially have an impact so if one is going for big mysteries unravelled it's something to bear in mind. <br /> <br /> But the fact is that jobs are just a thing humans do. You can't have a job spirit without that being a type of human spirit. A spirit of guide dogs is a spirit of dogs that happens to have specialised. A police spirit would be no different. At best it would be <i>message</i> delivery, rule enforcement and so on. What they do rather than who they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:00:10-07:00","id":455786,"title":"","content":"well gender is a social construct, and we already have spirits of other human concepts like freedom, so I don't see why there wouldn't be spirits with influences of masculinity, femininity, and/or androgyny. &quot;Gender Spirits&quot;, I imagine, would just have some combination of those. Humans aren't the only animals with sex hormones, so there could probably be spirits of testosterone and estrogen. Most animals have some form of sexual dimorphism, so there could be spirits of sexes. I'm not sure how faces are restricted to humans. My dogs have faces. While the conceptual baggage we attach to parenthood and siblinghood are human-created, the genetic connections exist among any life forms that reproduce sexually, so I'm positive those spirits would exist, and humans would just affect what influences those spirits might have. As for specific people, I would say no. But I suppose there may be spiritual reflections of the mythos that arise around famous historical figures. There may, for example, be a spirit of honesty that goes around attacking cherry tree spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:07:00-07:00","id":455808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455740#post455740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the fact is that jobs are just a thing humans do. You can't have a job spirit without that being a type of human spirit. A spirit of guide dogs is a spirit of dogs that happens to have specialised. A police spirit would be no different. At best it would be <i>message</i> delivery, rule enforcement and so on. What they do rather than who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are murder spirits, and murder is a very specific sort of thing that humans do. Providing you keep in mind murder is different from killing. In the Predators book, the playground spirit has an influence of Children, which seems like it would be a specific type of human spirit, since it's not referring to spider children. And the unihar are of course spirits of Uratha and hatred. Uratha aren't human but they are pretty close. Ancestor spirits are spirits of family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:15:58-07:00","id":455810,"title":"","content":"There are murder spirits. There are not any murder<i>er</i> spirits. Or assassin spirits. Or executioner spirits. It's a very subtle line, but it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:38:24-07:00","id":455821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455810#post455810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are murder spirits. There are not any murder<i>er</i> spirits. Or assassin spirits. Or executioner spirits. It's a very subtle line, but it's there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you say that, though? There's a spirit of Sinners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:49:07-07:00","id":455823,"title":"","content":"Which book is that in? <br /> <br /> Actually, how would that even work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:51:07-07:00","id":455825,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness: Chicago, it's an avatar of Amemet, the Eater of the Dead. It eats sinners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T07:58:22-07:00","id":455829,"title":"","content":"That doesn't sound much like a spirit <i>of</i> sinners at all, to be honest. You wouldn't call something that ate police officers a spirit of police, would you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:11:31-07:00","id":455835,"title":"","content":"It has a resonance of Sinners. As an avatar of a higher Hisil being, as far as I can tell it can be created however they want. There's also the Relict Men, the Hollow Men, and we already mentioned the Uratha spirits and ancestor spirits.<br /> <br /> Why are <i>you </i>saying that the limit is at jobs? Why is there a bank spirit, banking spirits, commerce spirits, money spirits, ATM spirits, the list goes on and on, but no banker spirit? Granted, there's no spirit of an individual teller, Tommy. But why wouldn't there be a banker spirit? What makes an unspecified ancestor spirit fine, but an unspecified banker spirit impossible to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:17:49-07:00","id":455837,"title":"","content":"Because I have difficulty justifying how that wouldn't count as a &quot;human spirit&quot; of some variety, which we are repeatedly told don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:25:04-07:00","id":455847,"title":"","content":"It's not a human. It has no existence outside of being a thing that opens accounts, hands you money or takes your money. Since the bank opened, people have gone there, paying little attention to the smiling face, turning down the offers to join a special checking plan or open a new account. Monday through Saturday, open to closing, there is a figure there to deal with customers. The names change, the people change, whatever. But there is someone doing that.<br /> <br /> In the Hisil, wouldn't there be something doing that? Again, no one specific, but just like an ancestral spirit is an 'ancestor' the banker spirit is a 'banker.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:35:44-07:00","id":455854,"title":"","content":"There <i>should </i>be. <br /> <br /> But there's not. <br /> <br /> It's not there. <br /> <br /> It's conspicuously absent. <br /> <br /> Just like there are no pedestrian spirits milling around in the streets. <br /> <br /> Just like there are no shopkeeper spirits tending the shadow's supermarkets. <br /> <br /> Just like there are no politician spirits arguing in the city hall. <br /> <br /> There are no people in the shadow. It seems abandoned. And a friendly face behind the screen at the bank is just one more thing missing from the place that makes it so eerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:40:44-07:00","id":455858,"title":"","content":"Are you basing this off of anything in the books, or is this your opinion? There's foot traffic spirits. And spirits can take human form. The bank spirit depicted in Predators, ' Because humanity has spent so much time conceptualizing about wealth, they are more likely than most buildings to take a human form. When doing so, they most often appear as the spirit\u2019s off-center conception of a banking executive, dressed well if the bank-spirit has been successful at gathering Essence, more shabbily if it is in decline.' So a bank is, at least, not empty. It appears as a person, it isn't a person, but so would a banker spirit.<br /> <br /> Also, the unihar exist as spirits of Uratha. Are there spirits of vampires? Prometheans? Mages? At what point do you become 'not human' enough to have a spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:52:38-07:00","id":455874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455858#post455858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the unihar exist</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any more they don't. <br /> <br /> I think as far as the WoD goes the other supernaturals provide a clear cutoff themselves. What is non-human enough to have a spirit? Something not human enough to be embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T08:57:48-07:00","id":455880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455874#post455874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think as far as the WoD goes the other supernaturals provide a clear cutoff themselves. What is non-human enough to have a spirit? Something not human enough to be embraced.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all of the major templates and some of the minor ones, like Purified and probably at least one other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:05:53-07:00","id":455886,"title":"","content":"Ok, I thought that was clear enough but obviously not. Allow me to clarify. <br /> <br /> What is non-human enough to have a spirit? Something not human enough to be embraced. Or Awaken. Or stolen by the Gentry. Or First-Change. Or become a mummy. Or be bound to a Geist. Or become human through an extensive soul transmutation process. Or have been a human at any point in their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:07:04-07:00","id":455887,"title":"","content":"So there are Uratha spirits, but no vampire spirits? That was my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:23:12-07:00","id":455931,"title":"","content":"The Uratha sprits are called the Uratha. Vampire's are so unspiritual that their spirits aren't actually spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-24-2015, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:25:46-07:00","id":455932,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, ancestor spirits are an Uratha thing; there are not human ancestor spirits. You might, however, get a spirit that has ended up attaching itself to a family over the ages due to a particular resonance and thus holds an 'ancestor' role - a murder-spirit that latched onto a family that has always had a violent and dark past, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> You don't get vampire spirits. Things like murder spirits, blood spirits, spirits of fear and hunger and the like, they will tend to flock to areas where vampires are at work, but the vampire will not itself have a direct spiritual reflection.<br /> <br /> I think it likely that, much like regular humans, Awakened don't have direct spiritual reflections (unless a Thyrsus just made themselves one I guess) but you'd absolutely have to check in with Dave B on that for clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T09:28:29-07:00","id":455933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455932#post455932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, ancestor spirits are an Uratha thing; there are not human ancestor spirits. You might, however, get a spirit that has ended up attaching itself to a family over the ages due to a particular resonance and thus holds an 'ancestor' role - a murder-spirit that latched onto a family that has always had a violent and dark past, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> You don't get vampire spirits. Things like murder spirits, blood spirits, spirits of fear and hunger and the like, they will tend to flock to areas where vampires are at work, but the vampire will not itself have a direct spiritual reflection.<br /> <br /> I think it likely that, much like regular humans, Awakened don't have direct spiritual reflections (unless a Thyrsus just made themselves one I guess) but you'd absolutely have to check in with Dave B on that for clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you think about the previous topic?<br /> There's murder spirits, but are there murderer spirits? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/455129-a-spirit-question?p=455847#post455847\">A banker spirit</a>? Assassin spirits? Are those too human to have spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:08:52-07:00","id":456009,"title":"","content":"There are spirits OF things. Your &quot;banker spirit&quot; would be a spirit of banking and would become more individualized as it gained power, it represents a concept, not people. A rule of thumb based on the previously written material is that if it has/had a soul then it desn't have a spiritual reflection in the Hisil. Corporations aren't people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divi